before:
```typescript
function formatCode(value: string | number): string {
  if (typeof value === "number") {
    return "Code " + (value + 1);
  }
  return "Code " + value;
}
console.log(formatCode(4));
console.log(formatCode("04"));
```

The calls print Code 5 and Code 04. formatCode receives text or a number and returns display text. typeof value === "number" is a runtime check; inside that branch value is numeric, so + 1 is arithmetic. After that branch returns, the remaining path handles text and keeps its leading zero.

after:
This function adds 1 only when the input is a number.
```typescript
function formatCode(value: string | number): string {
  if (typeof value === "number") {
    return "Code " + (value + 1);
  }
  return "Code " + value;
}
console.log(formatCode(4));
```
The output is Code 5.
